References: <20050503142246.2A7881008539@mailgate.biostat.wustl.edu>
Message-ID: <OFC3C33B84.C58715E1-ON86256FFC.004C353E-86256FFC.004C9FC5@usgs.gov>

Hi,

  Sorry, I deleted the original
posting before I realized how to respond to this posting.

  The difference between anova()
and summary(), which causes the call to by() to fail is that anova() extracts
the model matrix from the object. The model matrix cannot be extracted
because the data is not available. This can easily be solved by adding
model=T to the call to glm().

Dave

