Joseph,
As you can see from the simple function below, the results from the two
models are not the same. I believe the difference is in the error
component of the two models, they are not the same.
John

function()
{
        y1 <- c(1:100)
        y2 <- y1 + rnorm(length(y1), 0, 20)
        diff <- y2 - y1
        fitY2Y1 <- lm(y2 ~ y1)
        fitdiff <- lm(diff ~ y1)
        print(summary(fitY2Y1))
        print(summary(fitdiff))
        return()
}

