Message-ID: <20050512010819.E5F6DF3972@mail.blarg.net>

Hello, Mark,

 

Yes, offset is not in scope within the
call of sapply to the function. 

You can pass offset in as a variable to
sapply:

 

sapply(changepoints,function(i,y) (i-y):(i-1),
y=offset)

 

or possibly by first writing it to a
database:

...

assign(where=0,”.offset”,value=offset)

sapply(changepoints,function(i) (i-.offset):(i-1)

...

Since Splus considers frame 0 to always be
in scope. This is the session frame/database and goes away at the end of the
session. It is always in scope and masks definitions in other locations such as
where=1, the working database. 

Thus, the value is available to you during
the current session and is deleted at the end of the session.

 

Tom Jagger

 

