	  Thanks for the interesting discussion and the fine summary.  I would 
quibble with only one issue:  Your use of the phrase "correct terms" at 
the end.  I would not say, "correct" but rather say something like, 
"more standard or perferred statistical terms".  Their use of the terms 
"dependent" and "independent" correctly follows established practice in 
that discipline.  However, if professionals in your discipline want to 
be understood by a wider audience, it might be wise to choose terms that 
do not conflict with common usage outside your discipline.  This seems 
to say the same thing you did with appropriate humility.

          Best Wishes,
          spencer graves

